00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:54,920
They smoothed over the surface so the math looked correct.

63
00:04:55,340 --> 00:05:00,400
Mathematically speaking, the final state of system one and system two are now geometrically identical.

64
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:13,460
Right. If a security auditor evaluates a predicate, meaning like a formal true or false statement regarding the system's safety based solely on that single moment in time, both systems return true.

65
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:15,500
They both appear perfectly safe to deploy.

66
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:19,040
But only system one is what the paper defines as admissible.

67
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:24,900
System two is a compromised object that merely mimics the appearance of an admissible one.

68
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:38,620
I was thinking about this for you, the listener, and it's kind of similar to judging the structural integrity of a massive suspension bridge by only looking at its final coat of paint and measuring its cross-section against the blueprint.

